<title>MEXICO: POLL - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up to 19.06 pct.</title>
<headline>POLL - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up to 19.06 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 35 basis points to 19.06 percent, and rates are also seen rising at longer terms, according to a Reuters survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     18.71	    19.06		     35 bps</p>
<p>    90-DAY     19.63	    20.23		     60 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    20.77	    21.12		     35 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     20.84	    21.03		     19 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 (2330 GMT)</p>
<p>((--Fatima Escobar, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559))</p>
